    "updated_at": "2022-12-02T07:11:58Z",
    "body": "I'm not sure I agree that we should suggest conditional bootstrapping as the default.\r\n\r\nIf you run into this, it's either due to:\r\n1. Having incorrectly installed Starship\r\n\tAs it is today, an error is clearly surfaced saying that `starship` isn't a valid command rather than silently continuing to not show Starship's prompt. Hiding any error would make it very hard to begin to troubleshoot for shell beginners, a significant and vocal subset of Starship's users.\r\n1. You share common configuration between systems\r\n\tIn this case, odds are that you understand the implications of what you're calling, and you should be able to figure out a way to make it conditionally initialize Starship.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
